THOUGHT: NullAway complains that the constructor `Button(ButtonStyle style)` does not guarantee initialization of the (implicitly @NonNull) field `style` on all control-flow paths, likely because `setStyle` could throw or be overridden. A simple fix is to assign the field directly in the constructor before calling any methods that might throw, ensuring `this.style` is definitely initialized. I’ll modify the constructor to set `this.style = style;` before `initialize()` and keep the rest unchanged.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '82,86s/public Button(ButtonStyle style) {
    initialize();
    setStyle(style);
    setSize(getPrefWidth(), getPrefHeight());
  }/public Button(ButtonStyle style) {
    this.style = style;
    initialize();
    setStyle(style);
    setSize(getPrefWidth(), getPrefHeight());
  }/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Button.java
```

